Ladybird now compiles an event handler content attribute on an SVG
element into the element’s event handler, as the HTML spec’s event
handler attribute change steps say for every element that includes
GlobalEventHandlers. The other engines do the same: Blink, in its
SVGElement::ParseAttribute(), looks the attribute up with HTMLElement::
EventNameForAttributeName(). Gecko’s SVGElement::AfterSetAttr() checks
IsEventAttributeName(). And WebKit’s SVGElement::attributeChanged()
looks it up with HTMLElement::eventNameForEventHandlerAttribute().
